{
  "id": "COMPOUND:18132 - PROTEIN:5864",
  "verbalization": "Lancifodilactone N is shown to interact with Caspase-5, a key protease involved in apoptosis and cell death, and this interaction is supported by multiple pathways leading to U373 MG, a highly metastatic cancer cell line. The evidence suggests that Lancifodilactone N may inhibit Caspase-5, which in turn could trigger apoptosis in U373 MG cells. The presence of multiple targets (Caspase-5, cholesta-5,7,8(14),22E-tetraen-3-one, and (-)-Duryne F) further supports a potential mechanism of action involving Caspase-5, with U373 MG being a downstream target in all these pathways. The final scores indicate a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, but the exact mechanism of Caspase-5 inhibition by Lancifodilactone N remains to be fully elucidated. The observed effect on U373 MG suggests that this compound may have therapeutic potential in cancers where Caspase-5 is dysregulated, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the clinical relevance.",
